course: dictionary
lesson: 13901
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. Lapdog is a good example. «Mia's little lapdog curled up on her lap all evening.» Here a lapdog is a small pet dog that likes to sit on people's laps.
explain: The second meaning is informal and is used as an insult. «The mayor's advisers were lapdogs, agreeing with every word he said.» There is no dog here at all. In this sense, a lapdog is a person who always obeys a more powerful person without thinking.
explain: How do you know which meaning to use? Look at the clues. Fur, a basket or a walk point to the pet. A leader, a boss or politics point to the insult. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Lapdog means a small pet dog that likes to sit on people's laps.
fact: «Lapdog» can also mean a person who always obeys a more powerful person without thinking.
fact: The second meaning is informal and is used as an insult, so use it with care.
fact: «The manager's lapdog never said no to him.» Here the word describes a person, not an animal.
fact: The same word can have two meanings, and the clues in the sentence show you which one to choose.
exercise: «Mia's little lapdog curled up on her lap all evening.» What is a lapdog in this sentence? | A kind of bed | A huge farm animal | A person who always obeys | *A small pet dog that likes to sit on laps
exercise: «The minister was only a lapdog, agreeing with everything the prime minister said.» What does lapdog mean here? | A tired worker | A small friendly animal | *A person who always obeys a more powerful person | A pet that sleeps by the fire
exercise: «Grandma's lapdog slept in its basket by the fire.» Which word is a clue that lapdog means a pet here? | obeyed | leader | politics | *basket
test: «The senator's lapdog voted every time the president asked.» Is lapdog a pet or an insult here? | A sleepy cat | *An insult for someone who obeys without thinking | A kind of food | A pet
test: «Every night, Sam's lapdog waits by the door for his walk.» What does lapdog mean here? | A person who obeys | *A small pet dog | A dog that is cross | A tired dog's bed
exam: Jo says, «The director is just a lapdog for the owners.» What does Jo mean by lapdog? | A small pet dog that sits on laps | A lap made of wool | *A person who obeys a more powerful person without thinking | An animal that loves cuddles
